{"status": "ok", "segs": [[5, "Which sign-in risk detection method is"], [7, "most effective for identifying"], [9, "impossible travel scenarios?"], [11, "Option A, protocol analysis."], [14, "Option B, location-based tracking with"], [17, "time analysis."], [18, "Option C, user behavior analytics."], [22, "Option D, device fingerprinting."], [26, "Correct answer, option B."], [28, "Location-based tracking with time"], [30, "analysis is crucial for detecting"], [31, "impossible travel scenarios in sign-in"], [34, "attempts. This method analyzes the"], [35, "geographic location and timing of"], [37, "successive sign-in attempts to identify"], [39, "patterns that would be physically"], [41, "impossible for a single user to achieve."], [43, "For example, it can detect when sign-ins"], [46, "occur from different continents within"], [47, "an un"], [49, "When configuring PIM notifications, what"], [52, "alert scenario cannot be monitored on?"], [54, "Option A, user password strength during"], [57, "activation."], [59, "Option B, failed role activation"], [61, "attempts."], [62, "Option C, roles activated without MFA."], [67, "Option D, roles assigned outside of PIM."], [72, "Correct answer, option A."], [74, "PIM provides extensive monitoring and"], [77, "alerting capabilities for role"], [78, "management and security-related events."], [80, "While it can track role assignments,"], [82, "activations, and security conditions"], [84, "like MFA usage, it doesn't have the"], [86, "capability to evaluate individual"], [88, "password strength during role"], [90, "activation. Password policy enforcement"], [92, "is handled by Azure AD's password"], [94, "policies, not PIM."], [97, "What happens to external user accounts"], [99, "when automatic user provisioning is"], [101, "configured between Azure AD and a SaaS"], [103, "application?"], [104, "Option A, external users are excluded"], [107, "from automatic provisioning."], [109, "Option B, external users are provisioned"], [112, "after admin approval."], [114, "Option C, external users are provisioned"], [117, "with limited permissions."], [119, "Option D, external users are"], [122, "automatically provisioned like internal"], [123, "users."], [126, "Correct answer, option A."], [128, "Automatic user provisioning between"], [130, "Azure AD and SaaS applications typically"], [133, "excludes external users by default. This"], [135, "is a security measure to prevent"], [137, "unauthorized access to connected"], [139, "applications. Organizations must"], [141, "manually provision external users to"], [143, "these applications when needed, allowing"], [145, "for better control and visibility over"], [147, "external user access. This approach"], [149, "helps maintain security and compliance"], [152, "by ensuring external users only get"], [154, "access to necessary resources."], [157, "Which Microsoft Defender for Identity"], [159, "component is responsible for monitoring"], [161, "domain controllers and collecting"], [163, "security logs? L. Option A, connector."], [166, "Option B,"], [168, "sensor."], [169, "Option C, portal. Option D, cloud"], [172, "service."], [174, "Correct answer, option B."], [177, "The Microsoft Defender for Identity"], [178, "sensor is a crucial component installed"], [180, "directly on domain controllers or ADFS"], [183, "servers. Captures and analyzes network"], [185, "traffic and forwards compressed data to"], [187, "the cloud service for analysis. The"], [189, "sensor monitors multiple data sources"], [191, "including network traffic, Windows"], [193, "events, and other telemetry to provide"], [195, "comprehensive security monitoring of the"], [198, "identity infrastructure."], [200, "When configuring Microsoft Defender for"], [202, "Identity sensor capacity, what is the"], [204, "recommended CPU core allocation for"], [207, "monitoring a domain controller handling"], [209, "100,000 packets per second?"], [212, "Option A, four cores."], [214, "Option B, one core."