[311, "What is the primary purpose of"], [313, "conducting regular access reviews in"], [315, "Microsoft Defender?"], [317, "Option A, to ensure users maintain"], [319, "appropriate access levels."], [321, "Option B, to test backup systems."], [324, "Option C, to improve system performance."], [328, "Option D, to generate compliance"], [330, "reports."], [332, "Correct answer, option A."], [335, "Regular access reviews are crucial for"], [337, "maintaining security hygiene by ensuring"], [339, "users only have access to resources they"], [342, "need for their current roles. This"], [343, "process helps organizations maintain"], [345, "compliance, reduce security risks, and"], [348, "implement the principle of least"], [350, "privilege effectively. Access reviews"], [352, "also help identify and remove"], [354, "unnecessary permissions that may have"], [356, "accumulated over time."], [358, "Which feature in Microsoft Defender for"], [360, "Identity would best help identify"], [362, "dormant but privileged accounts that"], [365, "could pose a security risk? Option A,"], [368, "entity behavior analytics."], [370, "Option B, lateral movement paths"], [372, "analysis."], [374, "Option C, network mapping report."], [377, "Option D, security principal"], [379, "reconnaissance report."], [382, "Correct answer, option A."], [384, "Entity behavior analytics in Microsoft"], [386, "Defender for Identity is specifically"], [388, "designed to track and analyze account"], [391, "activity patterns over time. It can"], [393, "identify privileged accounts that"], [395, "haven't been used for extended periods,"], [397, "which could indicate forgotten accounts"], [399, "that pose security risks. This feature"], [401, "uses machine learning to establish"], [402, "baseline behaviors and can flag accounts"], [404, "that deviate from normal usage patterns,"], [407, "making it ideal for identifying dormant"], [409, "privileged accounts that should be"], [410, "reviewed or disabled."], [413, "What is the minimum permission required"], [414, "for the Microsoft Defender for Identity"], [416, "service account during sensor"], [418, "installations? Option A, domain admin"], [421, "rights."], [422, "Option B, enterprise admin rights."], [425, "Option C, server operator rights."], [428, "Option D, local administrator rights on"], [430, "domain controllers."], [433, "Correct answer, option D."], [435, "Microsoft Defender for Identity sensor"], [437, "installation requires local"], [439, "administrator rights on the domain"], [440, "controllers where the sensors will be"], [442, "installed. This follows the principle of"], [444, "least privilege while providing"], [446, "sufficient access for installation and"], [448, "configuration. Higher-level permissions"], [450, "like domain admin or enterprise admin"], [452, "are not necessary and could pose"], [454, "security risks if compromised. After"], [456, "installation, the service account can"], [458, "operate with reduced privileges for"], [460, "ongoing operations."], [462, "In Microsoft Defender's pass-through"], [464, "authentication, what is the first step"], [467, "to troubleshoot when users cannot"], [469, "authenticate? L. Option A, check the"], [472, "authentication agent service status."], [474, "Option B, contact Microsoft support."], [478, "Option C, reinstall Azure AD Connect."], [481, "Option D, reset the user's password."], [486, "Correct answer, option A."], [488, "When troubleshooting pass-through"], [489, "authentication issues, checking the"], [491, "authentication agent service status is"], [493, "the crucial first step. This verifies if"], [496, "the basic infrastructure for"], [497, "authentication is functioning properly."], [499, "The service status can be checked in the"], [501, "Windows services console on servers"], [503, "where the authentication agents are"], [505, "installed. If the service is stopped or"], [507, "showing errors, this often indicates the"], [509, "root cause of authentication problems."], [512, "When installing a pass-through"], [514, "authentication agent in Microsoft"], [515, "Defender,"], [517, "which prerequisite is mandatory for the"], [518, "server where the agent will be"], [520, "installed?"], [521, "Option A, the server must have a public"], [524, "IP address."], [525, "Option B, TLS 1.2 or later must be"], [529, "enabled."], [530, "Option C, the server must be a domain"], [533, "controller."], [534, "Option D, SQL Server must be installed."], [539, "Correct answer, option B."], [541, "Pass-through authentication agents"], [542, "require TLS 1.2 or later to establish"], [546, "secure communications with Azure AD."], [548, "This is crucial for protecting"], [549, "authentication traffic between"], [551, "on-premises and cloud environments. The"], [553, "agent can be installed on any"], [554, "domain-joined Windows server that meets"], [556, "the minimum requirements, including"], [558, "having TLS 1.2 enabled. The server"], [561, "doesn't need to be a domain controller"], [563, "or have specific roles like SQL Server"], [565, "installed."], [567, "In Microsoft Defender's pass-through"], [569, "authentication, which security measure"], [572, "prevents brute-force attacks against"], [574, "on-premises accounts?"], [576, "Option A, password hash synchronization."], [579, "Option B, smart lockout policy."], [582, "Option C, account lockout policy."], [585, "Option D, IP-based rate limiting."], [590, "Correct answer, option C."], [592, "In pass-through authentication, the"], [594, "on-premises Active Directory account"], [596, "lockout policy is the primary mechanism"], [598, "that protects against brute-force"], [600, "attacks. When an attacker attempts"], [602, "multiple failed login attempts, the"], [604, "account lockout policy configured in"], [606, "Active Directory will trigger,"], [608, "preventing further authentication"], [609, "attempts for the specified lockout"], [611, "duration."], [612, "This security measure is enforced"], [613, "regardless of whether the authentication"], [615, "attempt comes through Azure AD or"], [617, "directly on premises."], [620, "A security administrator needs to"], [622, "configure Microsoft Defender for"], [624, "Identity to detect lateral movement"], [626, "paths that could compromise sensitive"], [628, "accounts. Which prerequisite must be"], [630, "met? Option A, install Microsoft"], [632, "Defender for Identity sensors."], [634, "Option B, configure NTLM authentication"], [637, "auditing."], [638, "Option C, enable cloud app security."], [642, "Option D, enable Windows Defender"], [644, "antivirus."], [647, "Correct answer, option B."], [650, "Detecting lateral movement paths in"], [651, "Microsoft Defender for Identity requires"], [653, "NTLM authentication auditing to be"], [656, "enabled. This auditing captures"], [657, "authentication traffic and helps"], [659, "identify potential paths attackers could"], [661, "use to move laterally through the"], [663, "network. Without NTLM auditing, the"], [665, "system cannot accurately map these"], [666, "potential attack paths, making it"], [668, "crucial for security administrators to"], [670, "enable this feature before implementing"], [672, "lateral movement detection."], [674, "A security analyst receives a create"], [677, "suspicious service creation alert from"], [679, "Microsoft Defender for Identity."], [682, "Which of the following actions should be"], [684, "prioritized first?"], [685, "Option A, immediately disable the"], [688, "service."], [689, "Option B, export all logs to SIEM."], [693, "Option C, reset the password of the"], [695, "affected account."], [697, "Option D, check the service properties"], [699, "and creation context."], [702, "Correct answer, option D."], [705, "When investigating a suspicious service"], [706, "creation alert, it's crucial to first"], [708, "understand the context and potential"], [710, "impact before taking any remediation"], [712, "actions. This includes examining the"], [714, "service properties, creation time,"], [716, "account used, and surrounding"], [718, "activities. This information helps"], [720, "determine if it's a legitimate business"], [722, "activity or a potential security threat,"], [725, "guiding appropriate response actions."], [728, "In Microsoft Defender, which"], [730, "certificate-based configuration provides"], [732, "the highest level of security for"], [734, "authenticating devices?"], [736, "Option A, self-signed certificates with"], [738, "basic constraints."], [740, "Option B, hardware-bound certificates"], [742, "with TPM protection."], [744, "Option C, user-generated certificates"], [747, "with password protection."], [748, "Option D, software-based certificates"], [751, "with extended key usage."], [754, "Correct answer, option B."], [757, "Hardware-bound certificates with TPM"], [759, "protection represent the most secure"], [760, "certificate-based authentication method"], [763, "in Microsoft Defender. The Trusted"], [764, "Platform Module, TPM, provides"], [767, "hardware-level security by storing"], [769, "cryptographic keys in a secure enclave,"], [771, "preventing extraction even if the system"], [773, "is compromised. This approach ensures"], [775, "that certificates cannot be copied or"], [777, "stolen, and the private keys never leave"], [779, "the TPM, making it highly resistant to"], [781, "sophisticated attacks."], [784, "What happens to existing user sessions"], [787, "when an administrator revokes a FIDO2"], [790, "security key in Microsoft Defender?"], [793, "Option A, all user sessions remain"], [795, "active until their normal expiration."], [798, "Option B, all active sessions for the"], [800, "user are immediately terminated and"], [802, "require re-authentication."], [804, "Option C, only the session that used the"], [806, "FIDO2 key is terminated."], [810, "Option D, sessions are allowed to"], [812, "continue but with limited access."], [816, "Correct answer, option B."], [818, "When a FIDO2 security key is revoked in"], [821, "Microsoft Defender, the system"], [823, "immediately terminates all active"], [824, "sessions for the affected user as a"], [826, "security measure. This comprehensive"], [828, "approach ensures that potentially"], [830, "compromised credentials cannot be used"], [832, "to maintain access to the system. Users"], [834, "must reauthenticate using an alternative"], [836, "method or a new security key to regain"], [839, "access."], [840, "This immediate revocation and session"], [842, "termination is crucial for maintaining"], [844, "security in cases of lost or stolen"], [846, "security keys."], [848, "In Microsoft Defender for Identity,"], [851, "which passwordless authentication method"], [853, "provides the highest security level"], [855, "while requiring the least"], [856, "infrastructure?"], [857, "Option A, security keys FIDO2."], [861, "Option B, Windows Hello for Business."], [864, "Option C, SMS one-time passcodes."], [868, "Option D, Microsoft Authenticator app"], [871, "with certificate-based authentication."], [875, "Correct answer, option D."], [878, "The Microsoft Authenticator app with"], [880, "certificate-based authentication"], [881, "represents the optimal balance of"], [883, "security and ease of deployment. It"], [885, "leverages public key cryptography and"], [886, "biometric capabilities of modern"], [888, "devices,"], [889, "does it require physical token"], [891, "distribution, works across multiple"], [893, "platforms, and integrates seamlessly"], [895, "with existing Azure AD infrastructure."], [898, "The solution also provides fishing"], [899, "resistance through certificate-based"], [901, "authentication while maintaining a"], [903, "simple user experience."], [906, "In Microsoft Defender, which dashboard"], [908, "provides real-time insights into the"], [910, "progress of active access review"], [912, "campaigns?"], [913, "Option A, activity log."], [916, "Option B, Co